1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,280
Listen to this sound at the end of a word.

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:04,320
J!

3
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:06,900
Two spellings can make it.

4
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:11,440
We can write ge, or we can write dge.

5
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:14,190
Say it with me.

6
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:15,400
J!

7
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:20,560
You hear it in cage, and you hear it in badge.

8
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:25,220
It is the same sound, but the spelling is different.

9
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,120
So how do we know which one to write?

10
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:34,000
Just like ch and tch, we look at the letter before it.

11
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,290
Here is the rule.

12
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:42,110
If the sound comes right after a short vowel, we write dge.

13
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,660
Listen.

14
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,480
B - a - dge.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:48,440
Badge!

16
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,740
That a is a short vowel, so this word takes dge.

17
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:55,800
Here are more.

18
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:57,460
Bridge.

19
00:00:58,820 --> 00:00:59,220
Judge.

20
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:01,020
Fudge.

21
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:06,120
They all have a short vowel first, and then dge.

22
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,800
In every other place, we simply write ge.

23
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:13,530
There are two of those places.

24
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,900
The first is after a long vowel.

25
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:24,150
Listen to cage.

26
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:28,960
The a says its own name, so it is long.

27
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:32,860
That means we only need ge.

28
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,460
Page.

29
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:36,440
Huge.

30
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:38,480
Stage.

31
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:42,510
The second is after a consonant.

32
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,710
Listen to large.

33
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:48,860
There is an r before the sound.

34
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,980
So we write ge again.

35
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:52,860
Change.

36
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:54,980
Orange.

37
00:01:57,220 --> 00:01:59,400
Now let's put the whole family together.

38
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:04,480
Do you remember duck, from our c, k and ck video?

39
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,580
And catch, from our ch and tch video?

40
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:10,440
Duck.

41
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:12,300
Catch.

42
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:14,400
Badge.

43
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:21,080
Ck, tch and dge all do the same job!

44
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:25,560
A short vowel at the end of a word needs a helper.

45
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,660
Once you can see it, you will spot it everywhere.

46
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,490
And here is the best part.

47
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:37,120
Ch and tch had nine rule breakers to remember.

48
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,880
But dge does not have any!

49
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:46,880
In longer words like village and message you will see just ge.

50
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:49,280
Listen to those endings.

51
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,880
They sound quiet and soft.

52
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:57,700
But in short words, you can trust dge every single time.

53
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:01,140
Now let's look at more dge words.

54
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:02,980
Badge.

55
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:04,660
Bridge.

56
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:06,480
Judge.

57
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,340
Fudge.

58
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:10,420
Hedge.

59
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:12,360
Edge.

60
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:17,070
Every one of them has a short vowel, and then dge.

61
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,330
And now let's look at the ge words.

62
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:22,460
Cage.

63
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:24,220
Page.

64
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:26,220
Huge.

65
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,180
Large.

66
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,100
Change.

67
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:32,080
Orange.

68
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:38,440
After a long vowel, or after a consonant, we write just ge.

69
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,050
Now it is your turn!

70
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:42,720
Here is the word.

71
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:43,940
Huge.

72
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:48,790
Do we write it with ge, or with dge?

73
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:53,180
It is ge!

74
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:56,680
The u is saying its own name, so it is a long vowel.

75
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,340
So let's remember it together.

76
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,780
After a short vowel we write dge.

77
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:09,560
After a long vowel or a consonant, just ge.

78
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:15,800
And the best part is that this rule has no tricky words at all!

79
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:21,220
You can find every rule and every sound in the English Learning app.

80
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:23,840
It is free, so start today!
